      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #39925.\n\nThe fused FlashKDA prefill path wraps its tensor in `(output, None)` even when `return_intermediate_states=False`. The KDA caller only unpacks when tracking SSM checkpoints, so untracked GLM-5.3-Flash prefill reaches gated RMSNorm with a tuple and fails on `x.shape`.\n\n## Modifications\n\nReturn the fused output tensor directly. Keep the intermediate-state Triton fallback and all routing guards unchanged. One production file changed; no kernel math or serving flags changed.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nManual validation on GB300 using a downstream `0.5.19+82357279cc` build with the same faulty function:\n\n- Real GPU kernel replay reproduced the tuple failure. The fixed output and updated SSM state are bitwise equal to the original tensor/state; gated norm succeeds with finite output.\n- GLM-5.3-Flash TP2/EP2, DeepGEMM, DFlash2 block8, radix cache disabled: original full-model run failed at `glm5_next.py:552 -> fused_norm_gate.py:295`; identical 128-token request after the patch returned HTTP 200 and generated 16 tokens.\n- 32/128/1024/2048/4096-token requests and a text chat request returned HTTP 200 after the patch.\n\nReproduction and environment: #39925. Upstream main was source-checked, not separately GPU-deployed. No task-accuracy suite or PD transport validation was run. GPU replay scripts/logs were kept outside this minimal patch.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable: removes a Python tuple wrapper without changing kernel work. Functional requests are not reported as throughput benchmarks.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Run repository pre-commit hooks on the changed file (Python 3.12; passed).\n- [x] Validation: manual real-GPU replay and model regression documented above; no new CI unit test included in this minimal patch.\n- [x] Documentation: no user-facing API or configuration change; reproduction is documented in the linked issue.\n- [x] Accuracy/speed scope: bitwise kernel output/state checks supplied; no model-accuracy or performance claim.\n- [x] Follow existing SGLang code style and keep the change limited to the return contract.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35194447870](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35194447870)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35194447587](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35194447587)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35194447761](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35194447761)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
